$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Non-migration reaction conditions (procedure
A): 6 The appropriate aryl iodide (0.25 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (2.8 mg, 0.0125
mmol), n-Bu4NCl (0.0694 g, 0.25 mmol), NaHCO3 (0.042 g, 0.5 mmol) and
ethyl acrylate (0.10 g, 1.0 mmol) in DMF (1 ml) under Ar at 100 °C were
stirred for the specified length of time. The reaction mixture was then
cooled to room temperature, diluted with diethyl ether (35 mL) and washed
with brine (30 mL). The aqueous layer was reextracted with diethyl ether
(15 mL). The organic layers were combined, dried (MgSO4), filtered, and
the solvent removed under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by
column chromatography on a silica gel column. Ethyl
E-3-(4-dimethylaminobiphen-2-yl)acrylate (3b). N,N-Dimethyl-3-iodo-4-
phenylaniline (4b) (80.8 mg, 0.25 mmol) was allowed to react with ethyl
acrylate under nonmigration reaction conditions (procedure A) for 1 d.
The reaction mixture was chromatographed using 5:1 hexanes/ethyl acetate
to afford 73.8 mg (100%) of the indicated compound as a yellow oil: 1H
NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.28 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H), 3.01 (s, 6H), 4.21 (q, J = 7.2
Hz, 2H), 6.39 (d, J = 15.6 Hz, 1H), 6.85 (dd, J = 8.8, 2.8 Hz, 1H), 6.97
(d, J = 2.8 Hz,1H), 7.24-7.34 (m, 4H), 7.38-7.42 (m, 2H), 7.77 (d, J =
16.0 Hz, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 14.4, 40.6, 60.4, 109.8, 114.7, 118.7,
126.8, 128.2, 130.0, 131.3, 131.6, 133.1, 140.2, 145.1, 149.8, 167.1; IR
(CH2Cl2) 2975, 2920, 1711, 1632, 1605, 1174 cm-1; HRMS m/z 295.1577
(calcd for C19H21NO2, 295.1572).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
