$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Palladium-Catalyzed Heck Coupling of
Pyridyl-Substituted Vinylsilane and Aryl Iodide. To a solution of
Pd2(dba)3•CHCl3 (2.6 mg, 0.0025 rnmol, 0.5 mol %) and
tri-2-furylpbosphine (2.3 mg, 0.01 mmol, 2 mol %) in THF (1.5 mL) were
added iodobenzene (112 mg, 0.55 mmol), 2-pyridyldimethyl(vinyl)silane (1)
(82 mg, 0.50 mmol), and triethylamine (61 mg, 0.60 mmol) at room
temperature under argon and the reaction mixture was stirred at 50°C for
24 h. After cooling to room temperature, toluene (5 mL) was added to the
reaction mixture. This mixture was extracted with 1 N aq HCl (6 x 10 mL).
The combined aqueous phase was neutralized by adding NaHCO3 and then was
extracted with EtOAc (3 x 30 mL). Drying over Na2SO4 and removal of the
solvents under reduced pressure. (E)-β-(2-pyridyldimethylsilyl)styrene
(2a), yield 111 mg, 93%, as a pale yellow oil. 1H NMR (300 MHz) δ 0.50
(s, 6 H), 6.65 (d, J= 19.2 Hz, 1 H), 7.02 (d, J= 19.2 Hz, 1 H), 7.21
(ddd, J= 6.9,4.8,2.1 Hz, 1 H), 7.26-7.36 (m, 3 H), 7.44-7.49 (m, 2 H),
7.54-7.62 (m, 2 H), 8.81 (dt, J= 5.1, 1.2 Hz, 1 H); 13C NMR (75 MHz) δ
-3.4, 122.9, 126.1, 126.6, 128.3, 128.6, 129.5, 134.1, 138.2'-145.9,
150.4, 167.0. IR (neat) 2959, 1605, 15.74, 1495, 1449, 1418, 1246 cm-1.
HRMS (EI) m/z caIcd for C15H17NSi: 239.1131, found 239.1122. Anal. Calcd
for C15H17NSi: C, 75.26; H, 7.16; N, 5.85. Found: C, 75.49; H, 7.25; N,
5.83.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, other ligands give lower yield
