$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reaction of iodobenzene with methyl acrylate catalyzed by [Pd(C6H5)Br2]2
[N(C3H7)4]2 (3) (Scheme 3).5 Iodobenzene (102 mg, 0.500 mmol), methyl
acrylate (86 mg, 1.0 mmol), tetrabutylammonium chloride (139 mg, 0.500
mmol), and sodium bicarbonate (105 mg, 1.25 mmol) were weighed into a
small vial. A solution of [Pd(C6H5)Br2]2 [N(C3H7)4]2 (3) (5.3 mg, 5.0
μmol) in anhydrous DMF (1.0 mL) was then added by syringe. The mixture
was stirred at 30 °C. After 18 h, the mixture was diluted in
dichloromethane and washed with water then brine. The organic layer was
dried over anhydrous MgSO4 and evaporated. The crude material was
purified by flash chromatography (5% ethyl acetate in hexane) to afford
78 mg (96 % yield) of spectroscopically pure trans-methyl cinnamate as a
white solid. trans-methyl cinnamate, Yield 78 mg 96 %
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, Heck reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ligandless, Anionic, Arylpalladium Halide Intermediates in the Heck
Reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Carrow, Brad P.; Hartwig, John. F.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2010), 132(1), 79-81

