$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To test the catalytic abilities of the imino
pincer palladium complexes 2 to promote the Heck reaction, we initially
examined the reaction of iodobenzene (8a) with methyl acrylate (9a)
(Table 1). The reaction proceeded smoothly when a combination of
1-methyl-2-piperidone (NMP) as the solvent and tributylamine (Bu3N) as
the base was used. Thus, the reaction of 8a with 9a was carried out in
NMP in the presence of 1.4 mol equiv of Bu3N and 1.0 mol % of the pincer
complex 2a at 100 °C for 2 h to give methyl trans-cinnamate (10) in 90%
yield. methyl trans-cinnamate (10).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, thermal, Heck reaction, optimized on catalysts
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM NCN Pincer Palladium Complexes: Their Preparation via a Ligand
Introduction Route and Their Catalytic Properties
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Takenaka, Kazuhiro; Minakawa, Maki; Uozumi, Yasuhiro
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2005), 127(35), 12273-12281

