E-3-(4-methylbiphen-2-yl)acrylate (3a). Compound 4a (73.5 mg, 0.25 mmol)
was allowed to react with ethyl acrylate under Jeffrey's reaction
conditions for 1 day. The reaction mixture was chromatographed using 7:1
hexanes/ethyl acetate to afford 61.9 mg (93 %) of the indicated compound
as a clear oil: 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.28 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H), 2.42 (s, 3H),
