$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The Heck reaction of aryl bromides with
styrene in the presence of catalysts 5a and 5b (Table 1). General
Procedure: An oven-dried Schlenk flask was charged under argon with
bromobenzene (527 μL, 784 mg 5.0 mmol), styrene (690 μL, 648 mg, 6.0
mmol), anhydrous KOAc (589 mg, 6.0 mmol) and DMA (5.0 mL). A solution of
catalyst 5a in DMA (4.48 x 10-4 M, 90 μL, 8.0 x 10-4 mol %) was then
added via syringe. The flask was sealed and placed in a 140 oC oil bath
controlled by a J-KEMP temperature controller and stirred for 24 h. After
cooling to rt, the reaction mixture was poured into water (200 mL) and
extracted with EtOAc (3 x 50 mL). The combined organic extracts were
washed with brine, dried with anhydrous Na2SO4, and concentrated.
Purification by flash chromatography on silica gel (hexanes/CH2Cl2 1:1)
gave trans-stilbene along with a trace amount of its regioisomer (790 mg,
87%). 4-Methyl-trans-stilbene 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.69 (d, 2 H, J
= 7.7 Hz), 7.61 (d, 2 H, J = 8.1 Hz), 7.54 (t, 2 H, J = 7.6 Hz), 7.44 (t,
1 H, J = 7.3 Hz), 7.36 (d, 2 H, J = 7.9 Hz), 7.30 (d, 1 H, J = 16.3 Hz),
7.26 (d, 1 H, J = 16.3 Hz), 2.55 (s, 3 H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ
137.85, 137.66, 134.89, 129.70, 128.92, 128.02, 127.66, 126.79, 126.75,
21.51 (One aromatic carbon is missing due to overlap).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
