$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM S14. 14 A hot 100 mL Schlenk flask equipped with a stirbar and a rubber
septum was attached to a double manifold and cooled under vacuum. The
flask was opened to air, and S13 (1.56 g, 3 mmol), vinylboronic acid MIDA
ester (660 mg, 3.6 mmol), palladium(II) acetate (34 mg, 0.15 mmol), and
2- Dicyclohexylphosphino-2′,6′-dimethoxybiphenyl (SPhos, 123 mg, 0.3
mmol) were added. The flask was evacuated and backfilled three times with
nitrogen, and dioxane was added (36 mL). K3PO4 was added (7.5 mL, 3.0 M
solution in H2O, sparged prior to use). The reaction was heated for 2 h
at 100 °C. The reaction mixture was then transferred to a separatory
funnel and diluted with 100mL of aqueous NaOH (1M) and 100 mL diethyl
ether. The mixture was extracted with diethyl ether (3 x 100 mL), and the
combined organic layers were dried (MgSO4), filtered, and concentrated in
vacuo. The product was purified using flash silica chromatography
(hexanes) and concentrated in vacuo. 1.09 g (92%) of a white solid. mp =
71-82 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.26 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 7.20 (dd, J
= 8.1, 1.8 Hz, 1H), 7.12 (d, J = 1.5 Hz, 1H), 6.66 (dd, J = 17.6, 10.9
Hz, 1H), 5.69 (dd, J = 17.6, 1.1 Hz, 1H), 5.17 (dd, J = 10.9, 1.1 Hz,
1H), 3.64 (t, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 2.92 - 2.79 (m, 2H), 2.37 - 2.27 (m, 1H),
2.21 (td, J = 11.2, 3.8 Hz, 1H), 2.00 - 1.84 (m, 3H), 1.72 - 1.61 (m,
1H), 1.52 - 1.17 (m, 7H), 0.89 (s, 9H), 0.74 (s, 3H), 0.04 (s, 3H), 0.02
(s, 3H); 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 140.4, 136.9, 136.7, 134.8, 126.8,
125.6, 123.4, 112.9, 81.7, 49.7, 44.6, 43.5, 38.7, 37.1, 30.9, 29.6,
27.2, 26.2, 25.9, 23.3, 18.1, 11.3, -4.5, -4.8; FTIR (cm-1): 3440, 2928,
1642; HRMS (EI) m/z, calcd for [C26H40OSi]: 396.2848; found: 396.2836.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
