$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of Indanones
(II). To an oven-dried, 2-5 mL Biotage microwave vial with microstirrer
is added carbonyl-ene product (0.08 mmol, 1 equiv),
1,2,2,6,6-pentamethylpiperidine (2 equiv) and PdCl2(PPh3)2 (1 mol%). The
vial is capped with a crimp-cap and heated to 150 °C for 20-25 minutes in
a Biotage microwave reactor. The reaction is diluted with an equal volume
of diethyl ether and poured into a separatory funnel. The ethereal layer
is washed with a saturated aqueous NH4Cl solution (2 x 2 mL). The aqueous
washes are back extracted with diethyl ether (1 X 4 mL). The organic
fractions are combined and washed with brine (1 x 2 mL), dried with
anhydrous MgSO4, filtered and concentrated in vacuo. The crude products
are purified via column chromatography on silica gel.
(2S,3S)-2-ethanoyl-3-p-tolyl-2,3-dihydro-1H-inden-1-one (6e) Compound 6e
was prepared according to the general procedure (II) using (25 mg, 0.072
mmol), PdCl2(PPh3)2 (~0.5 mg, 1 mol%) and 1,2,2,6,6-pentamethylpiperidine
(26 μL, 0.145 mmol) in DMF (1.0 mL). The crude material was purified by
column chromatography (15% Ethyl Acetate:hexanes) to give the title
compound as a white solid (18 mg, 92%) 90% ee by HPLC using Chiralcel
OD-H, 0.2 mL/min, 0.5% 2-propanol in hexane tR = 13.27 (minor) and 16.62
(major) min (UV 254 nm). FTIR (film) 3428, 2919, 2850, 1657, 1599, 1466,
1383, 1290, 1244, 893, 801, 741 cm-1. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 14.07
(bs, 1H), 7.83 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.46 (ddd, J = 7.5, 7.5, 1.0 Hz, 1H),
7.39 (ddd, J = 7.5, 7.5, 0 Hz, 1H), 7.21 (d, J = 7.5 Hz, 1H), 7.10 (d, J
= 8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.03 (d, J = 8.0 Hz, 2H), 4.81 (s, 1H), 2.31 (s, 3H), 1.84
(s, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 193.2, 178.0, 153.0, 137.9,
136.7, 133.5, 129.6(2C), 127.63(2C), 127.58(2C), 125.6, 123.0, 115.7,
47.8, 21.0, 20.8 ppm. MS (ESI) m/z calcd for [M+Na]+ (C18H16O2Na)+: 287
Found: [M+Na]+ 287.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Enantioselective Synthesis of Substituted Indanones from Silyloxyallenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
