$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure. The synthesis of 1 is given
as reference. In a 35 mL pressure tube, triethoxyvinylsilane (1.17 mL,
5.38 mmol) was added to an aqueous sodium hydroxide 0.50 M solution (13.5
mL, 6.75 mmol) containing a 20% (w/w) of PEG 2000 (2.7 g). The mixture
was vigorously stirred for 5 min at room temperature and
1-(4-bromophenyl)ethanone (0.2742 g, 1.35 mmol) and palladium(II) acetate
(0.3 mg, 1.4 μmol) were subsequently added. The tube was subsequently
introduced into a silicone bath, previously warmed to 140 °C, and
vigorously stirred for 3 h. Once this time elapsed, the reaction mixture
was allowed to cool to room temperature and extracted with ethyl acetate
(3 × 20 mL). The combined organic layers were dried over MgSO4 and, after
filtration, the solvent eliminated in a rotary evaporator connected to a
water aspirator pump. The purification was performed by column
chromatography on silica gel using a mixture of hexane/ethyl acetate as
eluent. 2-Vinylnaftalene (6). 7 Following the general procedure,
triethoxyvinylsilane (0.44 mL, 2.15 mmol), an aqueous sodium hydroxide
solution 0.50 M (5.0 mL, 2.5 mmol), PEG 2000 (1.00 g), 2-bromonaftalene
(0.1067 g, 0.50 mmol) and palladium(II) acetate (0.6 mg, 2.7 μmol) were
warmed for 3 h at 140 °C. The final product was obtained as a white solid
(0.0709 g, 92%) after extraction with ethyl acetate and purification by
flash chromatography on silica gel with hexane as eluent. (R f = 0.34).
M. p.: 57-59 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ 5.32 (d, 1 H, 3 J c,a= 10.9;
Hc), 5.86 (d, 3 J b,a= 17.4, 1 H; Hb), 6.87 (dd, 3 J a,b= 17.4, 3 J a,c=
10.9,1 H; Ha), 7.39-7.48 (m, 2 H; H6, H7), 7.62 (dd, 3 J 3,4= 8.6, 4 J
3,1 = 1.6, 1 H; H3), 7.74-7.81 (m, 4 H; H1, H4, H5, H8). 13C{1H} NMR
(CDCl3): δ 114.1 (CH2), 123.1, 125.9, 126.2, 126.3, 127.6, 128.0, 128.1,
133.1, 133.5, 134.9, 136.9. EI-MS (70 eV): m/z (%) 154 (100) [M+], 128
(14), 76 (20). IR (KBr): ν 3054 w, 3020 m, 2974 m, 2926 m, 1919 w, 1810
w, 1685 w, 1625 m, 1595 m, 1572 w, 1507 m, 1438 m, 1416 w, 1361 m, 1274
m, 1176 w, 1124 m, 1105 m, 1082 m, 1017 w, 992 s, 965 m, 950 m, 896 s,
861 s, 821 s, 771 m, 750 s, 697 w, 617 w.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM thermal, Heck reaction, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mechanistic Studies on the Pd-Catalyzed Vinylation of Aryl Halides with
Vinylalkoxysilanes in Water: The Effect of the Solvent and NaOH Promoter
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gordillo, Alvaro; Ortuno, Manuel A.; Lopez-Mardomingo, Carmen; Lledos,
Agusti; Ujaque, Gregori; de Jesus, Ernesto
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2013), 135(37), 13749-13763

