$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Intramolecular
Asymmetric Heck Cyclizations. Preparation of
(S)-1-Benzyl-3-(2-methoxyvinyl)-3-phenyl-1,3-dihydroindol-2-one, (S)-12.
A base-washed and oven-dried 10 mL sealable tube equipped with a magnetic
stir bar was charged with 10 (98 mg, 0.19 mmol, 1.0 equiv), PMP (0.14 mL,
0.78 mmol, 4.0 equiv), and THF (0.8 mL). This solution was deoxygenated
by bubbling Ar through a submerged needle for 20 min, and Pd(OAc)2 (2.2
mg, 9.7 μmol, 5 mol %) and (R)-BINAP (12 mg, 19 μmol, 10 mol %) were then
added. Deoxygenation and vigorous stirring were continued for 15 min,
during which time a red solution resulted. The tube then was sealed and
heated at 80 °C for 6 h. After cooling to room temperature, the solution
was diluted with EtOAc (10 mL) and washed with NaHCO3 (3 × 10 mL). The
organic layer was dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated. The residue
was purified by flash chromatography (9:1 hexanes-ethyl acetate).
1-Benzyl-3-(2-methoxyvinyl)-3-naphthalen-1-yl-1,3-dihydroindol-2-one
(18d). The general procedure for the Heck cyclization was followed using
11d (90 mg, 0.16 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (2 mg, 8 μmol, 5 mol%), (R)-BINAP (10
mg, 16 μmol, 10 mol%), and PMP (120 μL, 0.65 mmol). Silica gel column
chromatograpy (hexanes-ethyl acetate, 9:1, v/v) of the crude residue gave
18d (61 mg, 0.15 mmol, 92%, 19:1 E/Z) as a colorless solid. [α]589 = +
67.3, [α]577 = + 70.3, [α]546 = + 79.8, [α]435 = + 146, [α]405 = + 184 (c
= 3.0 in CHCl3); 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.98 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 7.84
(t, J = 8.5 Hz, 2H), 7.57-7.51 (m, 3H), 7.43-7.33 (m, 4H), 7.23 (ddd, J =
8.0, 8.0, 1.5 Hz, 1H), 7.03 (m, 3H), 6.92 (ddd, J = 7.5, 7.5, 1.0 Hz,
1H), 6.86 (d, J = 6.5 Hz, 1H), 6.21 (d, J = 13.0 Hz, 1H), 5.54 (d, J =
13.0 Hz, 1H), 5.22 (d, J= 15.0 Hz, 1H), 5.02 (d, J = 15.0 Hz, 1H), 3.69
(s, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 178.7, 150.2, 141.8, 136.1, 134.6,
132.7, 131.2, 129.3, 128.2, 129.0, 128.7, 128.4, 128.3, 128.0, 127.8,
126.3, 125.5, 125.2, 124.9, 124.2, 122.9, 109.9, 105.8, 57.3, 56.7, 44.5;
IR (neat) 3053, 2934, 2856, 1714, 1648, 1610, 1486, 1467, 1339, 1216
cm-1; HRMS (CI) calcd for C28H23NO2: 405.1729; found: 405.1733.
