$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Non-migration reaction conditions (procedure
A): 6 The appropriate aryl iodide (0.25 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (2.8 mg, 0.0125
mmol), n-Bu4NCl (0.0694 g, 0.25 mmol), NaHCO3 (0.042 g, 0.5 mmol) and
ethyl acrylate (0.10 g, 1.0 mmol) in DMF (1 ml) under Ar at 100 °C were
stirred for the specified length of time. The reaction mixture was then
cooled to room temperature, diluted with diethyl ether (35 mL) and washed
with brine (30 mL). The aqueous layer was reextracted with diethyl ether
(15 mL). The organic layers were combined, dried (MgSO4), filtered, and
the solvent removed under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by
column chromatography on a silica gel column. Ethyl
E-3-(2’-methylbiphen-2-yl)acrylate (17). Compound 16 (73.5 mg, 0.25 mmol)
was allowed to react with ethyl acrylate under non-migration reaction
conditions (procedure A) for 1 d. The reaction mixture was
chromatographed using 7:1 hexanes/ethyl acetate to afford 61.2 mg (92%)
of the indicated compound 17 as a yellow oil: 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.24 (t, J
= 7.2 Hz, 3H), 2.03 (s, 3H), 4.16 (q, v = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 6.33 (d, J = 16.0
Hz, 1H), 7.10 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 7.20-7.29 (m, 4H), 7.37-7.44 (m, 3H),
7.70-7.72 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 14.3, 20.1, 60.4, 119.0, 125.7,
126.2, 127.7, 128.0, 129.8, 129.9, 130.1, 130.5, 133.0, 136.1, 139.6,
142.9, 143.0, 166.9; IR (CH2Cl2) 3061, 2978, 2920, 1713, 1633, 1177 cm-1;
HRMS m/z 266.1312 (calcd for C18H18O2, 266.1307).
