$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Suzuki-Type Reactions Using Ru/Alumina as a
Catalyst. To a solution of 4'-iodoacetophenone (246.1 mg, 1.0 mmol) in
1,2- dimethoxyethane/water (v, 1:1, 1.0 mL) was added phenylboronic acid
(182.9 mg, 1.5 mmol), NaOH (80.0 mg, 2.0 mmol), and Ru/Al2O3 (5 wt %,
20.2 mg, 0.01 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at 60 °C, and the
progress of the reaction was monitored by TLC until 4'- iodoacetophenone
disappeared completely. After 12 h, the reaction mixture was diluted with
EtOAc (10 mL), followed by water (10 mL). The organic layer was
separated, washed with aqueous NaHCO3 and NaOH solution (5%) several
times, and then dried over anhydrous MgSO4. The organic layer was
filtered through a pad of silica gel. After removal of organic solvent
under reduced pressure, the residue was purified by flash column
chromatography (ethyl acetate/hexane, 1:20) to give 4-phenylacetophenone
(184 mg, 99%). Table 3, entry 6, yield 91%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling, catalyst on Al2O3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
