$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the 1,4-palladium alkyl
to aryl migration. A mixture of aryl halide (0.25 mmol), Pd(OAc)2 (2.8
mg, 0.0125 mmol), bis(diphenylphosphino)methane (4.8 mg, 0.0125 mmol),
cesium pivalate (0.1170 g, 0.5 mmol), and the indicated amounts of alkene
(if employed) in dry DMF (4 mL) was quickly flushed with argon and
stirred at the indicated reaction temperature. The reaction was monitored
by TLC and gas chromatographic analysis. After the reaction was complete,
it was diluted with ethyl ether, washed with satd aq NaHCO3, dried over
Na2SO4, concentrated, and purified by flash chromatography on silica gel.
5-Methoxy-12b-methyl-1,12b-dihydro-2H-benzo[5,6]indeno[1,2,3-de]chromene
(10). The reaction mixture was chromatographed using 10:1 hexane/EtOAc to
afford 69 mg of the indicated compound (91 % yield) as a white solid: mp
58-61 °C; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 1.50 (s, 3H), 1.71-1.83 (m, 1H), 2.34-2.39 (m,
1H), 4.53-4.58 (m, 1H), 4.61- 4.70 (m, 1H), 6.36 (d, J = 2.1 H, 1H), 6.95
(d, J = 2.1 Hz, 1H), 7.44-7.47 (m, 2H), 7.78 (s, 1H), 7.81-7.84 (m, 1H),
7.87-7.91 (m, 1H), 8.07 (s, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 27.1, 31.9, 41.6,
56.0, 65.8, 99.1, 100.4, 119.5, 121.6, 125.9, 126.0, 128.2, 128.5, 133.2,
133.6, 139.1, 140.4, 152.4, 153.5, 162.2 (one sp2 carbon missing due to
overlap); IR (CHCl3, cm-1) 3018, 2963, 2922, 1612, 1596, 1483; HRMS Calcd
for C21H18O2: 302.1307. Found: 302.1312.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Pd-Catalyzed Alkyl to Aryl Migration and Cyclization: An Efficient
Synthesis of Fused Polycycles via Multiple C-H Activation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Huang, Qinhua; Fazio, Alessia; Dai, Guangxiu; Campo, Marino A.; Larock,
Richard C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2004), 126(24), qamca7460-7461

